     \\"score\\": 0.42521,\\n          \\"score\\": 0.44494,\\n          \\"score\\": 0.44494,\\n          \\"score\\": 0.461,\\n          \\"score\\": 0.461,\\n          \\"score\\": 0.46875,\\n          \\"score\\": 0.46875,\\n          \\"score\\": 0.50045,\\n          \\"score\\": 0.50045,\\n          \\"score\\": 0.51551,\\n          \\"score\\": 0.51551,\\n          \\"score\\": 0.66825,\\n          \\"score\\": 0.66825,\\n          \\"score\\": 0.73471,\\n          \\"score\\": 0.73471,\\n          \\"score\\": 0.75435,\\n          \\"score\\": 0.75435,\\n          \\"score\\": 0.85209,\\n          \\"score\\": 0.85209,\\n",\n  "duration_ms": 201,\n  "exit_code": 0,\n  "output_dir": "/tmp/nexau_bash_tool_results/27b478f9",\n  "stdout_file": "/tmp/nexau_bash_tool_results/27b478f9/stdout.txt",\n  "stderr_file": "/tmp/nexau_bash_tool_results/27b478f9/stderr.txt"\n}'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "Perfect! I can see the hit score distribution:\n- Negative hits: -0.41614, -0.33204\n- Positive hits: 0.38417, 0.42521, 0.44494, 0.461, 0.46875, 0.50045, 0.51551, 0.66825, 0.73471, 0.75435, 0.85209\n\nThe current thresholds are:\n- Positive boost: > 0.1 (works well, captures all positive hits)\n- Negative boost: < -0.2 (works for the two negative hits at -0.416 and -0.332)\n\nHowever, I notice that the negative threshold at -0.2 might be too conservative. Looking at the evolution, candidate 2 penalized moderately negative scores (between -0.1 and -0.2), which was then changed in candidate 3 to boost only strongly negative scores (<-0.2).\n\nBut what about moderately negative scores between -0.2 and -0.1? Currently they get no boost. Looking at the hit at -0.332, we might want to also boost scores around -0.15 to -0.2 range.\n\nHowever, I want to make a more targeted improvement. Looking at the current model, I notice that when boosting probabilities, it uses:\n- For positive: `sampled_prob *= (1.0 + avg_score)`\n- For negative: `sampled_prob *= (1.0 + abs(avg_score